i> favors the brave, but I guess it favors persistence as well. Fine... Here you go: In a world where everything is designed to catch your attention and squeeze your dopamine receptors dry, you’ll join <i>Cubert</i> in his everlasting journey of completing just one more lap. And, much like life (in case the laps metaphor wasn’t clear enough), there might just be something more awaiting for you at the start of the next one.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>¿ Y ? play this game, then:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this <strong>three-act, short Sisyphean walking narrative</strong>, you’ll uncover the answers to the very questions that set <i>Cubert</i> off on his journey in the first place. As the story unfolds, you’ll face a series of <strong>challenges and minigames</strong> that will shift and mirror the protagonist’s inner turmoil.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Roll through a <strong>condensed, introspective experience</strong> designed to be played in a single session, one that invites you to confront your own existential questions along the way.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pay close attention to what is being said  for hidden within this <strong>minimalistic world</strong> are the clues to what’s yet to come. </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
